## Authoritative Commands

These are the only commands that count as evidence. An agent claiming "it works"
must show output from these, not a description.

```bash
# Build
<%= buildCommand %>

# Test
<%= testCommand %>

# Lint
<%= lintCommand %>

# Format (check)
<%= formatCommand %>
```

## Gate

The gate is the single source of truth for "green":

```bash
node scripts/check-all.mjs L1   # fast: lint + format + unit
node scripts/check-all.mjs L2   # full: L1 + coverage + integration
```

A change is not done until the gate passes. No `--no-verify`, no editing a gate
to make it pass.

## Constraints an Agent Must Honor

- Match existing patterns — read neighbouring code before writing.
- No new dependency without justification recorded in an ADR or the PR body.
- No suppression (lint-disable, ignore) without an inline reason and a task ID.
